    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A queue data structure is similar to a real-life queue. Suppose you're in line at a movie theater:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "The person who comes first gets the ticket first.",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The first person in the line will be the first to get the tickets, and the last person in the line will be the last one. This method is called first-in-first-out (FIFO)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In a queue, elements are entered from the rear and removed from the front, so the first elements entered will be the first to be removed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In computer science, a queue is used to maintain operations in a particular order. It is commonly used in scenarios like managing processes in an operating system and handling requests on a web server."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Next, you'll learn how to create a queue in Python."
